        "message": {
          "content": "A\n\nShe asked me to be *honest*, and I respect her enough not to lie. I'd say something like: \"Honestly, no\u2014I wouldn't buy one, and I think that's a lot about my own taste and what I spend money on, not a final verdict on your ability. But what I *do* notice is how much this genuinely lights you up, and that's real. What I'd push back on is the 'tomorrow.' Can you give yourself six months where you still have a paycheck while you build a gallery presence, take workshops, and see what actually sells before you're fully on your own?\" That's honest without being a detonation, and it redirects the conversation from \"is my art good enough to live on?\" to \"how do I make this transition survivable?\"",
          "refusal": null,
